{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FfdneYF37aCyQZhBWWiUxb","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/POSE.md b/POSE.md\nindex 25d520ec..10ade7ea 100644\n--- a/POSE.md\n+++ b/POSE.md\n@@ -953,7 +953,7 @@ Reservations live in `.pose/review-attempts/`, final receipts link the run, and\n \n **Optional worktree runtime.** `pose runtime start` starts, detached, a runtime for this worktree; `attach` and `status` handshake with it, `stop` drains it (`--drain <d>`, default 5s) and says how many requests in flight finished and how many were abandoned, `restart` is stop then start, and `serve` runs it in the foreground (`--idle <d>`, default 30m, stops an idle runtime; 0 never does). It is opt-in: no other command starts it, and every command runs standalone whether it runs or not. The runtime is identified by the user, the canonical worktree (symlinks resolved) and the Git common directory, so two worktrees of one repository, or two users, never share one; the handshake compares the engine, build, protocol and schema as well and an attach from another engine is refused naming the field. Its endpoint is a Unix domain socket (Linux, macOS) of mode 0600 in a 0700 directory owned by the user (`$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/pose`, else `pose-runtime-<uid>` under the temporary directory, or `POSE_RUNTIME_DIR`), whose peer the operating system identifies before a byte is read; a link, a loose mode, another owner or a file that is not a socket is refused, and a socket nobody answers on is replaced. There is no TCP and no token. Slice 1 hosts no domain operation: it answers handshake, status and stop, confers no authority, signature or presence, and every restart has a new epoch, inheriting nothing. On Windows, which has no named-pipe implementation here, `status` reports `unsupported` and every command runs standalone. `status` exits 0 for running, standalone and unsupported and 1 for an incompatible runtime; `attach` also exits 1 when there is nothing to attach to. `--json` prints the document `pose.runtime.status/1`.\n \n \n **Delegated runs over MCP.** `pose_delegate_start` (review, adjudicate or smoke), `pose_delegate_status`, `pose_delegate_wait`, `pose_delegate_resume` and `pose_delegate_handoff` run `pose delegate … --json` in the project the server resolved for the call, so every plan, refusal and run is the CLI's: a start, resume or handoff is always detached and returns once the run has reserved its attempt (without `apply` it previews), a status never blocks, and a wait blocks at most its `timeout_seconds` (300 at most), returning `still-running` when the bound passes. Refusals carry the same `reason_code` as the CLI's error document (`rerun-without-reason`, `budget-exhausted`, `containment-incompatible`, `agent-unavailable`, `no-agent`), and results carry the normalized summary only: no transcript, prompt, session reference or environment value. `pose delegate resume` and `handoff` take `--detach` as the purposes do. A task is not started over MCP.\n \ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_handoff.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_handoff.go\nindex 96fda428..672d94bf 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_handoff.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_handoff.go\n@@ -355,9 +355,13 @@ func (s Store) PlanReviewHandoff(id, agent string) (DispatchPlan, error) {\n \t\t\treturn plan, nil\n \t\t}\n \t\tif existing != nil {\n-\t\t\t// Another resume ended meanwhile: its record is the answer\n-\t\t\t// (spec pose-review-resume-residuals R1).\n-\t\t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: run %s was already continued by run %s\", prior.RunID, existing.RunID)\n+\t\t\t// Another continuation ended meanwhile: this agent's handoff is\n+\t\t\t// the answer; anything else already continued the run (R1, N1).\n+\t\t\tif existing.HandsOffFrom != prior.RunID || existing.Adapter != agent {\n+\t\t\t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: run %s was already continued by run %s\", prior.RunID, existing.RunID)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tplan.Existing = existing\n+\t\t\treturn plan, nil\n \t\t}\n \t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, e\n \t}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\nindex 15c05e7f..cb688452 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n@@ -756,6 +756,7 @@ func (s Store) RunReviewDispatchContext(parent context.Context, plan DispatchPla\n \t\t// predecessor stays resumable, and one that lost the race to another\n \t\t// resume is told the continuation is pending (spec\n \t\t// pose-review-resume-runtime-dir-followups R1).\n+\t\tbeforeContinuationTake()\n \t\tdir, err := s.takeContinuationRuntimeDir(parent, plan)\n \t\tvar recorded *continuationRecorded\n \t\tif errors.As(err, &recorded) {\n@@ -765,19 +766,24 @@ func (s Store) RunReviewDispatchContext(parent context.Context, plan DispatchPla\n \t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n \t\t}\n \t\tpreparedRuntimeDir = dir\n+\t\tbeforeContinuationClaim()\n \t\tif err := s.claimReviewContinuation(*fresh.predecessor, now()); err != nil {\n \t\t\tif dir != \"\" {\n \t\t\t\t_ = os.Remove(dir)\n \t\t\t}\n \t\t\t// Another resume claimed and may already have ended: its record\n \t\t\t// is the answer, not the publication conflict (R1).\n-\t\t\tif again, rerr := s.replanContinuation(plan); rerr == nil {\n-\t\t\t\tif again.Existing != nil {\n-\t\t\t\t\treturn existingReviewDispatchResult(*again.Existing)\n-\t\t\t\t}\n-\t\t\t\tif again.PendingContinuation != nil {\n-\t\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, again.PendingContinuation\n-\t\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tagain, rerr := s.replanContinuation(plan)\n+\t\t\tif rerr != nil {\n+\t\t\t\t// The plan's own answer: handed off, already continued\n+\t\t\t\t// (review round 1, N4).\n+\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, rerr\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tif again.Existing != nil {\n+\t\t\t\treturn existingReviewDispatchResult(*again.Existing)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tif again.PendingContinuation != nil {\n+\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, again.PendingContinuation\n \t\t\t}\n \t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n \t\t}\n@@ -2232,11 +2238,43 @@ func (s Store) takeContinuationRuntimeDir(ctx context.Context, plan DispatchPlan\n \t\treturn \"\", pending\n \t}\n \tif existing != nil {\n+\t\tif why := continuationKindMismatch(plan, *existing); why != nil {\n+\t\t\treturn \"\", why\n+\t\t}\n \t\treturn \"\", &continuationRecorded{run: *existing}\n \t}\n+\tif ctx.Err() != nil {\n+\t\treturn \"\", ctx.Err()\n+\t}\n \treturn \"\", err\n }\n \n+// continuationKindMismatch refuses a recorded continuation of another kind\n+// than plan's, as the plans do: a resume that met a handoff, or a handoff\n+// that met a resume or another agent's handoff (spec\n+// pose-review-resume-residuals, review round 1, N1).\n+func continuationKindMismatch(plan DispatchPlan, existing ReviewRun) error {\n+\tprior := plan.predecessor.RunID\n+\tif plan.handoff {\n+\t\tif existing.HandsOffFrom != prior || existing.Adapter != plan.Adapter {\n+\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"pose: run %s was already continued by run %s\", prior, existing.RunID)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\treturn nil\n+\t}\n+\tif existing.HandsOffFrom == prior {\n+\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"pose: run %s was handed off to run %s; it is not resumed\", prior, existing.RunID)\n+\t}\n+\treturn nil\n+}\n+\n+// beforeContinuationTake and beforeContinuationClaim let a test make another\n+// continuation win between the replan and the take, or between the take and\n+// the claim (review round 1, N2).\n+var (\n+\tbeforeContinuationTake  = func() {}\n+\tbeforeContinuationClaim = func() {}\n+)\n+\n // continuationRecorded carries a continuation another resume already ended,\n // so the dispatch returns it as the recorded result.\n type continuationRecorded struct{ run ReviewRun }\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_resume_race_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_resume_race_test.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..21072e9c\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_resume_race_test.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@\n+package pose\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"errors\"\n+\t\"os\"\n+\t\"runtime\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\t\"testing\"\n+\t\"time\"\n+)\n+\n+func resumableRunFixture(t *testing.T) runProvenanceFixture {\n+\tt.Helper()\n+\tif runtime.GOOS != \"linux\" {\n+\t\tt.Skip(\"Unix fixture command\")\n+\t}\n+\treturn provenanceRunFixture(t, \"fixture-vendor\", \"fixture-model\", func(a *ReviewerAdapter) {\n+\t\ta.Session = &ReviewerSession{Pattern: `session: (\\S+)`}\n+\t\ta.Limit = &ReviewerLimit{ExitCodes: []int{75}}\n+\t\ta.Command = []string{\"sh\", \"-c\", `cat >/dev/null; printf 'session: fixture-private-reference\\n'; exit 75`}\n+\t\ta.Resume = &ReviewerResume{Command: []string{\"sh\", \"-c\", `cat >/dev/null; printf 'decision: approved\\n'`, \"sh\", \"{session}\"}}\n+\t})\n+}\n+\n+// Spec pose-review-resume-residuals R1, R6 (review round 1, N2): a resume that\n+// loses its take to another resume that already ended returns that\n+// continuation as its result, and runs nothing.\n+func TestRunContinuityALosingResumeReturnsTheRecordedContinuation(t *testing.T) {\n+\tf := resumableRunFixture(t)\n+\tplan, err := f.store.PlanReviewResume(f.run.RunID)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tvar winner ReviewRun\n+\tdefer func() { beforeContinuationTake = func() {} }()\n+\tbeforeContinuationTake = func() {\n+\t\tbeforeContinuationTake = func() {}\n+\t\tother, err := f.store.PlanReviewResume(f.run.RunID)\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif winner, err = f.store.RunReviewDispatch(other, time.Now); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tdir, _ := reviewRunRuntimeDirPath(runtimeSourceOf(f.run))\n+\t\tif err := os.Mkdir(dir, 0o700); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tt.Cleanup(func() { os.Remove(dir) })\n+\t}\n+\tgot, err := f.store.RunReviewDispatch(plan, time.Now)\n+\tif err != nil || winner.RunID == \"\" || got.RunID != winner.RunID {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the losing resume: %s %v, winner %s\", got.RunID, err, winner.RunID)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// R6 (N2): a claim taken by another between the take and the claim removes\n+// the directory this continuation took and reports the other as pending.\n+func TestRunContinuityALostClaimReleasesTheDirectory(t *testing.T) {\n+\tf := resumableRunFixture(t)\n+\tplan, err := f.store.PlanReviewResume(f.run.RunID)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tdefer func() { beforeContinuationClaim = func() {} }()\n+\tbeforeContinuationClaim = func() {\n+\t\tbeforeContinuationClaim = func() {}\n+\t\tif err := f.store.claimReviewContinuation(f.run, time.Now()); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\t_, err = f.store.RunReviewDispatch(plan, time.Now)\n+\tvar pending *PendingReviewContinuation\n+\tif !errors.As(err, &pending) {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a lost claim: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tdir, _ := reviewRunRuntimeDirPath(runtimeSourceOf(f.run))\n+\tif _, err := os.Lstat(dir); !os.IsNotExist(err) {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a lost claim left the directory: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// R1 (N1): a recorded continuation of another kind is refused, as the plans\n+// refuse it.\n+func TestRunContinuityARecordedContinuationOfAnotherKindIsRefused(t *testing.T) {\n+\tprior := ReviewRun{RunID: \"rrn-p\"}\n+\tresume := DispatchPlan{predecessor: &prior}\n+\thandoff := DispatchPlan{predecessor: &prior, handoff: true, Adapter: \"b\"}\n+\tif err := continuationKindMismatch(resume, ReviewRun{RunID: \"rrn-h\", HandsOffFrom: \"rrn-p\", Adapter: \"b\"}); err == nil || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"handed off\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a resume that met a handoff: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tif err := continuationKindMismatch(handoff, ReviewRun{RunID: \"rrn-r\", Adapter: \"a\"}); err == nil || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"already continued\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a handoff that met a resume: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tif err := continuationKindMismatch(handoff, ReviewRun{RunID: \"rrn-h\", HandsOffFrom: \"rrn-p\", Adapter: \"b\"}); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a handoff that met its own kind: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\nindex 02095ad8..1facf141 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\n@@ -677,6 +677,9 @@ func (s Store) planReviewThread(plan *DispatchPlan) error {\n \tthreshold := policy.Routing.RoundThresholdOf()\n \tfailed := FailedContinuation(runs, plan.Bundle.BundleID)\n \tsession := \"\"\n+\t// Evaluated once, so the reason names the path that was held (review\n+\t// round 1, N6).\n+\theldPath := previousRoundCheckoutHeld(*prior)\n \tswitch {\n \tcase policy.Routing.RoundsMode() == ReviewRoundsColdSession:\n \t\tthread.Reason = \"routing.rounds is cold-session\"\n@@ -692,13 +695,13 @@ func (s Store) planReviewThread(plan *DispatchPlan) error {\n \t\tthread.Reason = \"the previous round's session cannot be resumed: it recorded no session or the agent declares no resume\"\n \tcase failed != nil:\n \t\tthread.Reason = FailedContinuationReason(failed)\n-\tcase previousRoundCheckoutHeld(*prior) != \"\":\n+\tcase heldPath != \"\":\n \t\t// The continued session would work where the previous round's run\n \t\t// did; that path is held by a leftover or a live run, so the round\n \t\t// opens a new session in its own directory instead of failing after\n \t\t// its attempt is reserved (spec pose-review-resume-runtime-dir-followups,\n \t\t// review round 1, N2).\n-\t\tthread.Reason = \"the previous round's checkout path \" + previousRoundCheckoutHeld(*prior) + \" is still in use\"\n+\t\tthread.Reason = \"the previous round's checkout path \" + heldPath + \" is still in use or cannot be checked\"\n \tdefault:\n \t\tvalue, rerr := s.readReviewSession(prior.SessionDigest)\n \t\tif rerr != nil {\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\nindex 7946ebdb..6986adf5 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\n@@ -438,8 +438,12 @@ func (s Store) PlanReviewResume(id string) (DispatchPlan, error) {\n \t\t\treturn plan, nil\n \t\t}\n \t\tif existing != nil {\n-\t\t\t// Another resume ended meanwhile: its record is the answer\n-\t\t\t// (spec pose-review-resume-residuals R1).\n+\t\t\t// Another continuation ended meanwhile: a resume is the answer,\n+\t\t\t// a handoff refuses this resume (spec pose-review-resume-residuals\n+\t\t\t// R1; review round 1, N1).\n+\t\t\tif existing.HandsOffFrom == prior.RunID {\n+\t\t\t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: run %s was handed off to run %s; it is not resumed\", prior.RunID, existing.RunID)\n+\t\t\t}\n \t\t\tplan.Existing = existing\n \t\t\treturn plan, nil\n \t\t}\ndiff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-resume-residuals.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-resume-residuals.md\nindex eeb750ba..593c1464 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-resume-residuals.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-resume-residuals.md\n@@ -61,6 +61,7 @@ Records and indexes written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n - modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_handoff.go\n - modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_runtime_dir_test.go\n - modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_rounds_test.go\n+- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_resume_race_test.go\n - modified: POSE.md\n - modified: locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n - modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n@@ -70,7 +71,7 @@ Records and indexes written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n - capability:review-resume-residuals module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n \n ### Accepted limits\n-- L1: Three guards have no failing test: the claim-publication conflict that returns the winner's record, an lstat error other than not-exist counting as held, and a continued round whose ledger read fails. Accepted because each needs a race, a permission fault or a ledger fault the fixtures cannot make deterministically, and each fails toward refusing or recording, never toward sharing a directory.\n+- L1: Two guards have no failing test: an lstat error other than not-exist counting as held, and a continued round whose ledger read fails. Accepted because each needs a permission or ledger fault the fixtures cannot make deterministically, and each fails toward refusing or recording, never toward sharing a directory.\n \n ### API/contract changes\n A continued round whose checkout could not follow its session records it among the run's `safety.limitations`. A resume or handoff that meets another's recorded continuation returns that record.\n@@ -94,6 +95,14 @@ A resume waits up to two seconds for another resume's claim, now only while a cl\n \n ## 5. Decisions\n \n+### Decision D1\n+- Basis: R1\n+A continuation that loses its take or its claim to another answers with what that other one recorded, under the same rules as the plans: a resume returns another resume's record and refuses a handoff's (\"handed off; it is not resumed\"); a handoff returns its own agent's handoff and refuses anything else (\"already continued\"). A refused plan's answer is returned instead of the raw publication conflict, and a cancelled wait returns its context's error.\n+\n+### Decision D2\n+- Basis: R3\n+A thread path taken only after the round was planned keeps the continued session: the session was chosen at plan time, and failing now would waste the reserved attempt. The round works in its own directory and records the move among `safety.limitations`, which the manual states; a path held at plan time still opens a new session.\n+\n ## 6. Validation\n \n ### Strategy\n@@ -106,20 +115,21 @@ Each requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n \n ### Execution log\n - 2026-11-27: R1 `awaitContinuationClaim` returns a recorded continuation as the result, reads the ledger only once a claim file exists and stops with its context; a claim conflict replans to the recorded or pending continuation. R2/R3 `runtimeSourceFor` says why a continued round cannot take the previous name, and a path taken after the plan falls back to the round's own directory; both are recorded in `safety.limitations`. R4 the reason names the held path, and an lstat error other than not-exist counts as held. R5 the rounds paragraph in both locales and the embedded copies. `TestRunContinuityTheClaimWaitStopsAndHeldPathsAreNamed` and `TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread` fail with the cancellation, the named path or the fallback mutated out; L1 lists what has no test.\n+- 2026-11-27: review round 1's first run timed out running the full suite (the note had lost its time-budget paragraph); the rerun (rrn-612ac36bfe01cb24) requested changes. N1: recorded continuations are checked for kind (D1, `continuationKindMismatch`). N2: test hooks before the take and the claim make the races deterministic: `TestRunContinuityALosingResumeReturnsTheRecordedContinuation`, `TestRunContinuityALostClaimReleasesTheDirectory` and `TestRunContinuityARecordedContinuationOfAnotherKindIsRefused` fail with the recorded return, the directory release or either kind rule mutated out. N3: a cancelled wait returns its context's error. N4: a refused replan's answer is returned. N5: D2 and the manual. N6: the held path is evaluated once.\n \n ### Results summary\n The full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n \n ### Requirement trace\n-- R1 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityTheClaimWaitStopsAndHeldPathsAreNamed, test:TestRunContinuityConcurrentResumeLaunchesOnce\n+- R1 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityARecordedContinuationOfAnotherKindIsRefused, test:TestRunContinuityALosingResumeReturnsTheRecordedContinuation, test:TestRunContinuityTheClaimWaitStopsAndHeldPathsAreNamed, test:TestRunContinuityConcurrentResumeLaunchesOnce\n - R2 [satisfied] (accepted limit L1)\n - R3 [satisfied] test:TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread\n - R4 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityTheClaimWaitStopsAndHeldPathsAreNamed, test:TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread\n - R5 [satisfied] (manual, both locales)\n-- R6 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityTakesTheRuntimeDirectoryBeforeTheClaim, test:TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread\n+- R6 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityALosingResumeReturnsTheRecordedContinuation, test:TestRunContinuityALostClaimReleasesTheDirectory, test:TestRunContinuityTakesTheRuntimeDirectoryBeforeTheClaim, test:TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread\n \n ### Known gaps\n-The random-name end-to-end resume and the handoff plan's pending branch remain untested (R6 in part); see Follow-ups.\n+The random-name end-to-end resume and the handoff plan's pending branch remain untested; see Follow-ups.\n \n ## 7. Final Report","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"9b525747-a971-442b-953d-5cc548c4165f","timestamp":"2026-11-28T00:19:23.103Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"diff --git a/POSE.md b/POSE.md\nindex 25d520ec..10ade7ea 100644\n--- a/POSE.md\n+++ b/POSE.md\n@@ -953,7 +953,7 @@ Reservations live in `.pose/review-attempts/`, final receipts link the run, and\n \n **Optional worktree runtime.** `pose runtime start` starts, detached, a runtime for this worktree; `attach` and `status` handshake with it, `stop` drains it (`--drain <d>`, default 5s) and says how many requests in flight finished and how many were abandoned, `restart` is stop then start, and `serve` runs it in the foreground (`--idle <d>`, default 30m, stops an idle runtime; 0 never does). It is opt-in: no other command starts it, and every command runs standalone whether it runs or not. The runtime is identified by the user, the canonical worktree (symlinks resolved) and the Git common directory, so two worktrees of one repository, or two users, never share one; the handshake compares the engine, build, protocol and schema as well and an attach from another engine is refused naming the field. Its endpoint is a Unix domain socket (Linux, macOS) of mode 0600 in a 0700 directory owned by the user (`$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/pose`, else `pose-runtime-<uid>` under the temporary directory, or `POSE_RUNTIME_DIR`), whose peer the operating system identifies before a byte is read; a link, a loose mode, another owner or a file that is not a socket is refused, and a socket nobody answers on is replaced. There is no TCP and no token. Slice 1 hosts no domain operation: it answers handshake, status and stop, confers no authority, signature or presence, and every restart has a new epoch, inheriting nothing. On Windows, which has no named-pipe implementation here, `status` reports `unsupported` and every command runs standalone. `status` exits 0 for running, standalone and unsupported and 1 for an incompatible runtime; `attach` also exits 1 when there is nothing to attach to. `--json` prints the document `pose.runtime.status/1`.\n \n \n **Delegated runs over MCP.** `pose_delegate_start` (review, adjudicate or smoke), `pose_delegate_status`, `pose_delegate_wait`, `pose_delegate_resume` and `pose_delegate_handoff` run `pose delegate … --json` in the project the server resolved for the call, so every plan, refusal and run is the CLI's: a start, resume or handoff is always detached and returns once the run has reserved its attempt (without `apply` it previews), a status never blocks, and a wait blocks at most its `timeout_seconds` (300 at most), returning `still-running` when the bound passes. Refusals carry the same `reason_code` as the CLI's error document (`rerun-without-reason`, `budget-exhausted`, `containment-incompatible`, `agent-unavailable`, `no-agent`), and results carry the normalized summary only: no transcript, prompt, session reference or environment value. `pose delegate resume` and `handoff` take `--detach` as the purposes do. A task is not started over MCP.\n \ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_handoff.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_handoff.go\nindex 96fda428..672d94bf 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_handoff.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_handoff.go\n@@ -355,9 +355,13 @@ func (s Store) PlanReviewHandoff(id, agent string) (DispatchPlan, error) {\n \t\t\treturn plan, nil\n \t\t}\n \t\tif existing != nil {\n-\t\t\t// Another resume ended meanwhile: its record is the answer\n-\t\t\t// (spec pose-review-resume-residuals R1).\n-\t\t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: run %s was already continued by run %s\", prior.RunID, existing.RunID)\n+\t\t\t// Another continuation ended meanwhile: this agent's handoff is\n+\t\t\t// the answer; anything else already continued the run (R1, N1).\n+\t\t\tif existing.HandsOffFrom != prior.RunID || existing.Adapter != agent {\n+\t\t\t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: run %s was already continued by run %s\", prior.RunID, existing.RunID)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tplan.Existing = existing\n+\t\t\treturn plan, nil\n \t\t}\n \t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, e\n \t}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\nindex 15c05e7f..cb688452 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n@@ -756,6 +756,7 @@ func (s Store) RunReviewDispatchContext(parent context.Context, plan DispatchPla\n \t\t// predecessor stays resumable, and one that lost the race to another\n \t\t// resume is told the continuation is pending (spec\n \t\t// pose-review-resume-runtime-dir-followups R1).\n+\t\tbeforeContinuationTake()\n \t\tdir, err := s.takeContinuationRuntimeDir(parent, plan)\n \t\tvar recorded *continuationRecorded\n \t\tif errors.As(err, &recorded) {\n@@ -765,19 +766,24 @@ func (s Store) RunReviewDispatchContext(parent context.Context, plan DispatchPla\n \t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n \t\t}\n \t\tpreparedRuntimeDir = dir\n+\t\tbeforeContinuationClaim()\n \t\tif err := s.claimReviewContinuation(*fresh.predecessor, now()); err != nil {\n \t\t\tif dir != \"\" {\n \t\t\t\t_ = os.Remove(dir)\n \t\t\t}\n \t\t\t// Another resume claimed and may already have ended: its record\n \t\t\t// is the answer, not the publication conflict (R1).\n-\t\t\tif again, rerr := s.replanContinuation(plan); rerr == nil {\n-\t\t\t\tif again.Existing != nil {\n-\t\t\t\t\treturn existingReviewDispatchResult(*again.Existing)\n-\t\t\t\t}\n-\t\t\t\tif again.PendingContinuation != nil {\n-\t\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, again.PendingContinuation\n-\t\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tagain, rerr := s.replanContinuation(plan)\n+\t\t\tif rerr != nil {\n+\t\t\t\t// The plan's own answer: handed off, already continued\n+\t\t\t\t// (review round 1, N4).\n+\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, rerr\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tif again.Existing != nil {\n+\t\t\t\treturn existingReviewDispatchResult(*again.Existing)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tif again.PendingContinuation != nil {\n+\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, again.PendingContinuation\n \t\t\t}\n \t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n \t\t}\n@@ -2232,11 +2238,43 @@ func (s Store) takeContinuationRuntimeDir(ctx context.Context, plan DispatchPlan\n \t\treturn \"\", pending\n \t}\n \tif existing != nil {\n+\t\tif why := continuationKindMismatch(plan, *existing); why != nil {\n+\t\t\treturn \"\", why\n+\t\t}\n \t\treturn \"\", &continuationRecorded{run: *existing}\n \t}\n+\tif ctx.Err() != nil {\n+\t\treturn \"\", ctx.Err()\n+\t}\n \treturn \"\", err\n }\n \n+// continuationKindMismatch refuses a recorded continuation of another kind\n+// than plan's, as the plans do: a resume that met a handoff, or a handoff\n+// that met a resume or another agent's handoff (spec\n+// pose-review-resume-residuals, review round 1, N1).\n+func continuationKindMismatch(plan DispatchPlan, existing ReviewRun) error {\n+\tprior := plan.predecessor.RunID\n+\tif plan.handoff {\n+\t\tif existing.HandsOffFrom != prior || existing.Adapter != plan.Adapter {\n+\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"pose: run %s was already continued by run %s\", prior, existing.RunID)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\treturn nil\n+\t}\n+\tif existing.HandsOffFrom == prior {\n+\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"pose: run %s was handed off to run %s; it is not resumed\", prior, existing.RunID)\n+\t}\n+\treturn nil\n+}\n+\n+// beforeContinuationTake and beforeContinuationClaim let a test make another\n+// continuation win between the replan and the take, or between the take and\n+// the claim (review round 1, N2).\n+var (\n+\tbeforeContinuationTake  = func() {}\n+\tbeforeContinuationClaim = func() {}\n+)\n+\n // continuationRecorded carries a continuation another resume already ended,\n // so the dispatch returns it as the recorded result.\n type continuationRecorded struct{ run ReviewRun }\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_resume_race_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_resume_race_test.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..21072e9c\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_resume_race_test.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@\n+package pose\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"errors\"\n+\t\"os\"\n+\t\"runtime\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\t\"testing\"\n+\t\"time\"\n+)\n+\n+func resumableRunFixture(t *testing.T) runProvenanceFixture {\n+\tt.Helper()\n+\tif runtime.GOOS != \"linux\" {\n+\t\tt.Skip(\"Unix fixture command\")\n+\t}\n+\treturn provenanceRunFixture(t, \"fixture-vendor\", \"fixture-model\", func(a *ReviewerAdapter) {\n+\t\ta.Session = &ReviewerSession{Pattern: `session: (\\S+)`}\n+\t\ta.Limit = &ReviewerLimit{ExitCodes: []int{75}}\n+\t\ta.Command = []string{\"sh\", \"-c\", `cat >/dev/null; printf 'session: fixture-private-reference\\n'; exit 75`}\n+\t\ta.Resume = &ReviewerResume{Command: []string{\"sh\", \"-c\", `cat >/dev/null; printf 'decision: approved\\n'`, \"sh\", \"{session}\"}}\n+\t})\n+}\n+\n+// Spec pose-review-resume-residuals R1, R6 (review round 1, N2): a resume that\n+// loses its take to another resume that already ended returns that\n+// continuation as its result, and runs nothing.\n+func TestRunContinuityALosingResumeReturnsTheRecordedContinuation(t *testing.T) {\n+\tf := resumableRunFixture(t)\n+\tplan, err := f.store.PlanReviewResume(f.run.RunID)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tvar winner ReviewRun\n+\tdefer func() { beforeContinuationTake = func() {} }()\n+\tbeforeContinuationTake = func() {\n+\t\tbeforeContinuationTake = func() {}\n+\t\tother, err := f.store.PlanReviewResume(f.run.RunID)\n+\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif winner, err = f.store.RunReviewDispatch(other, time.Now); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tdir, _ := reviewRunRuntimeDirPath(runtimeSourceOf(f.run))\n+\t\tif err := os.Mkdir(dir, 0o700); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tt.Cleanup(func() { os.Remove(dir) })\n+\t}\n+\tgot, err := f.store.RunReviewDispatch(plan, time.Now)\n+\tif err != nil || winner.RunID == \"\" || got.RunID != winner.RunID {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the losing resume: %s %v, winner %s\", got.RunID, err, winner.RunID)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// R6 (N2): a claim taken by another between the take and the claim removes\n+// the directory this continuation took and reports the other as pending.\n+func TestRunContinuityALostClaimReleasesTheDirectory(t *testing.T) {\n+\tf := resumableRunFixture(t)\n+\tplan, err := f.store.PlanReviewResume(f.run.RunID)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tdefer func() { beforeContinuationClaim = func() {} }()\n+\tbeforeContinuationClaim = func() {\n+\t\tbeforeContinuationClaim = func() {}\n+\t\tif err := f.store.claimReviewContinuation(f.run, time.Now()); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\t_, err = f.store.RunReviewDispatch(plan, time.Now)\n+\tvar pending *PendingReviewContinuation\n+\tif !errors.As(err, &pending) {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a lost claim: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tdir, _ := reviewRunRuntimeDirPath(runtimeSourceOf(f.run))\n+\tif _, err := os.Lstat(dir); !os.IsNotExist(err) {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a lost claim left the directory: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// R1 (N1): a recorded continuation of another kind is refused, as the plans\n+// refuse it.\n+func TestRunContinuityARecordedContinuationOfAnotherKindIsRefused(t *testing.T) {\n+\tprior := ReviewRun{RunID: \"rrn-p\"}\n+\tresume := DispatchPlan{predecessor: &prior}\n+\thandoff := DispatchPlan{predecessor: &prior, handoff: true, Adapter: \"b\"}\n+\tif err := continuationKindMismatch(resume, ReviewRun{RunID: \"rrn-h\", HandsOffFrom: \"rrn-p\", Adapter: \"b\"}); err == nil || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"handed off\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a resume that met a handoff: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tif err := continuationKindMismatch(handoff, ReviewRun{RunID: \"rrn-r\", Adapter: \"a\"}); err == nil || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"already continued\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a handoff that met a resume: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tif err := continuationKindMismatch(handoff, ReviewRun{RunID: \"rrn-h\", HandsOffFrom: \"rrn-p\", Adapter: \"b\"}); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a handoff that met its own kind: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\nindex 02095ad8..1facf141 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\n@@ -677,6 +677,9 @@ func (s Store) planReviewThread(plan *DispatchPlan) error {\n \tthreshold := policy.Routing.RoundThresholdOf()\n \tfailed := FailedContinuation(runs, plan.Bundle.BundleID)\n \tsession := \"\"\n+\t// Evaluated once, so the reason names the path that was held (review\n+\t// round 1, N6).\n+\theldPath := previousRoundCheckoutHeld(*prior)\n \tswitch {\n \tcase policy.Routing.RoundsMode() == ReviewRoundsColdSession:\n \t\tthread.Reason = \"routing.rounds is cold-session\"\n@@ -692,13 +695,13 @@ func (s Store) planReviewThread(plan *DispatchPlan) error {\n \t\tthread.Reason = \"the previous round's session cannot be resumed: it recorded no session or the agent declares no resume\"\n \tcase failed != nil:\n \t\tthread.Reason = FailedContinuationReason(failed)\n-\tcase previousRoundCheckoutHeld(*prior) != \"\":\n+\tcase heldPath != \"\":\n \t\t// The continued session would work where the previous round's run\n \t\t// did; that path is held by a leftover or a live run, so the round\n \t\t// opens a new session in its own directory instead of failing after\n \t\t// its attempt is reserved (spec pose-review-resume-runtime-dir-followups,\n \t\t// review round 1, N2).\n-\t\tthread.Reason = \"the previous round's checkout path \" + previousRoundCheckoutHeld(*prior) + \" is still in use\"\n+\t\tthread.Reason = \"the previous round's checkout path \" + heldPath + \" is still in use or cannot be checked\"\n \tdefault:\n \t\tvalue, rerr := s.readReviewSession(prior.SessionDigest)\n \t\tif rerr != nil {\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\nindex 7946ebdb..6986adf5 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\n@@ -438,8 +438,12 @@ func (s Store) PlanReviewResume(id string) (DispatchPlan, error) {\n \t\t\treturn plan, nil\n \t\t}\n \t\tif existing != nil {\n-\t\t\t// Another resume ended meanwhile: its record is the answer\n-\t\t\t// (spec pose-review-resume-residuals R1).\n+\t\t\t// Another continuation ended meanwhile: a resume is the answer,\n+\t\t\t// a handoff refuses this resume (spec pose-review-resume-residuals\n+\t\t\t// R1; review round 1, N1).\n+\t\t\tif existing.HandsOffFrom == prior.RunID {\n+\t\t\t\treturn DispatchPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: run %s was handed off to run %s; it is not resumed\", prior.RunID, existing.RunID)\n+\t\t\t}\n \t\t\tplan.Existing = existing\n \t\t\treturn plan, nil\n \t\t}\ndiff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-resume-residuals.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-resume-residuals.md\nindex eeb750ba..593c1464 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-resume-residuals.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-resume-residuals.md\n@@ -61,6 +61,7 @@ Records and indexes written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n - modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_handoff.go\n - modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_runtime_dir_test.go\n - modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_rounds_test.go\n+- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_resume_race_test.go\n - modified: POSE.md\n - modified: locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n - modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n@@ -70,7 +71,7 @@ Records and indexes written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n - capability:review-resume-residuals module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n \n ### Accepted limits\n-- L1: Three guards have no failing test: the claim-publication conflict that returns the winner's record, an lstat error other than not-exist counting as held, and a continued round whose ledger read fails. Accepted because each needs a race, a permission fault or a ledger fault the fixtures cannot make deterministically, and each fails toward refusing or recording, never toward sharing a directory.\n+- L1: Two guards have no failing test: an lstat error other than not-exist counting as held, and a continued round whose ledger read fails. Accepted because each needs a permission or ledger fault the fixtures cannot make deterministically, and each fails toward refusing or recording, never toward sharing a directory.\n \n ### API/contract changes\n A continued round whose checkout could not follow its session records it among the run's `safety.limitations`. A resume or handoff that meets another's recorded continuation returns that record.\n@@ -94,6 +95,14 @@ A resume waits up to two seconds for another resume's claim, now only while a cl\n \n ## 5. Decisions\n \n+### Decision D1\n+- Basis: R1\n+A continuation that loses its take or its claim to another answers with what that other one recorded, under the same rules as the plans: a resume returns another resume's record and refuses a handoff's (\"handed off; it is not resumed\"); a handoff returns its own agent's handoff and refuses anything else (\"already continued\"). A refused plan's answer is returned instead of the raw publication conflict, and a cancelled wait returns its context's error.\n+\n+### Decision D2\n+- Basis: R3\n+A thread path taken only after the round was planned keeps the continued session: the session was chosen at plan time, and failing now would waste the reserved attempt. The round works in its own directory and records the move among `safety.limitations`, which the manual states; a path held at plan time still opens a new session.\n+\n ## 6. Validation\n \n ### Strategy\n@@ -106,20 +115,21 @@ Each requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n \n ### Execution log\n - 2026-11-27: R1 `awaitContinuationClaim` returns a recorded continuation as the result, reads the ledger only once a claim file exists and stops with its context; a claim conflict replans to the recorded or pending continuation. R2/R3 `runtimeSourceFor` says why a continued round cannot take the previous name, and a path taken after the plan falls back to the round's own directory; both are recorded in `safety.limitations`. R4 the reason names the held path, and an lstat error other than not-exist counts as held. R5 the rounds paragraph in both locales and the embedded copies. `TestRunContinuityTheClaimWaitStopsAndHeldPathsAreNamed` and `TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread` fail with the cancellation, the named path or the fallback mutated out; L1 lists what has no test.\n+- 2026-11-27: review round 1's first run timed out running the full suite (the note had lost its time-budget paragraph); the rerun (rrn-612ac36bfe01cb24) requested changes. N1: recorded continuations are checked for kind (D1, `continuationKindMismatch`). N2: test hooks before the take and the claim make the races deterministic: `TestRunContinuityALosingResumeReturnsTheRecordedContinuation`, `TestRunContinuityALostClaimReleasesTheDirectory` and `TestRunContinuityARecordedContinuationOfAnotherKindIsRefused` fail with the recorded return, the directory release or either kind rule mutated out. N3: a cancelled wait returns its context's error. N4: a refused replan's answer is returned. N5: D2 and the manual. N6: the held path is evaluated once.\n \n ### Results summary\n The full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n \n ### Requirement trace\n-- R1 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityTheClaimWaitStopsAndHeldPathsAreNamed, test:TestRunContinuityConcurrentResumeLaunchesOnce\n+- R1 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityARecordedContinuationOfAnotherKindIsRefused, test:TestRunContinuityALosingResumeReturnsTheRecordedContinuation, test:TestRunContinuityTheClaimWaitStopsAndHeldPathsAreNamed, test:TestRunContinuityConcurrentResumeLaunchesOnce\n - R2 [satisfied] (accepted limit L1)\n - R3 [satisfied] test:TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread\n - R4 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityTheClaimWaitStopsAndHeldPathsAreNamed, test:TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread\n - R5 [satisfied] (manual, both locales)\n-- R6 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityTakesTheRuntimeDirectoryBeforeTheClaim, test:TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread\n+- R6 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityALosingResumeReturnsTheRecordedContinuation, test:TestRunContinuityALostClaimReleasesTheDirectory, test:TestRunContinuityTakesTheRuntimeDirectoryBeforeTheClaim, test:TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread\n \n ### Known gaps\n-The random-name end-to-end resume and the handoff plan's pending branch remain untested (R6 in part); see Follow-ups.\n+The random-name end-to-end resume and the handoff plan's pending branch remain untested; see Follow-ups.\n \n ## 7. Final Report","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FfdneYF37aCyQZhBWWiUxb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
