{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P5kZot3yruph8RoMKpMD3S","type":"tool_result","content":"40:- R6: Tests shall reach the exclusive take after a replan, resume end to end a run whose recorded random name differs from the stable one, and cover the claim-failure removal and the handoff plan's pending branch (rounds 1 N3, 2 N8).\n74:- L1: Two guards have no failing test: an lstat error other than not-exist counting as held, and a continued round whose ledger read fails. Accepted because each needs a permission or ledger fault the fixtures cannot make deterministically, and each fails toward refusing or recording, never toward sharing a directory.\n77:A continued round whose checkout could not follow its session records it among the run's `safety.limitations`. A resume or handoff that meets another's recorded continuation returns that record.\n98:### Decision D1\n102:### Decision D2\n129:- R6 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityALosingResumeReturnsTheRecordedContinuation, test:TestRunContinuityALostClaimReleasesTheDirectory, test:TestRunContinuityTakesTheRuntimeDirectoryBeforeTheClaim, test:TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread\n132:The random-name end-to-end resume and the handoff plan's pending branch remain untested; see Follow-ups."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"a97b652d-f01e-47e8-9a69-cf0277b5b907","timestamp":"2026-11-28T00:28:08.791Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"40:- R6: Tests shall reach the exclusive take after a replan, resume end to end a run whose recorded random name differs from the stable one, and cover the claim-failure removal and the handoff plan's pending branch (rounds 1 N3, 2 N8).\n74:- L1: Two guards have no failing test: an lstat error other than not-exist counting as held, and a continued round whose ledger read fails. Accepted because each needs a permission or ledger fault the fixtures cannot make deterministically, and each fails toward refusing or recording, never toward sharing a directory.\n77:A continued round whose checkout could not follow its session records it among the run's `safety.limitations`. A resume or handoff that meets another's recorded continuation returns that record.\n98:### Decision D1\n102:### Decision D2\n129:- R6 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityALosingResumeReturnsTheRecordedContinuation, test:TestRunContinuityALostClaimReleasesTheDirectory, test:TestRunContinuityTakesTheRuntimeDirectoryBeforeTheClaim, test:TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread\n132:The random-name end-to-end resume and the handoff plan's pending branch remain untested; see Follow-ups.","numLines":7,"totalLines":7},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01P5kZot3yruph8RoMKpMD3S","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChUNwG4VGRPCLTrHNgGMo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Lf6PMQa6YNRNq6KNVK4GVy","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat <<'EOF' > \"$TMPDIR/draft.md\"\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n```pose-draft\n{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"changes-requested\",\n\"findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"R1-N2\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\".pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-resume-residuals.md\",\"line\":129,\"summary\":\"R6 is still traced satisfied but half of it is missing: no test resumes end to end a run with a recorded random runtime name (only the unit naming test), and none reaches the handoff plan's pending branches (delegation_handoff.go:331-337 and 353-356 uncovered); Known gaps admits both. L1 was also narrowed to two guards, yet the claim-conflict return of the winner's record that it used to accept still has no covering test (review_dispatch.go:782-784), as do the replan refusal (777-781) and the plan-level recorded returns and kind rules (review_run_continuity.go:440-448, delegation_handoff.go:357-364, wiring at review_dispatch.go:2241-2243).\"},\n{\"id\":\"R1-N3\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go\",\"line\":435,\"summary\":\"The take path now returns the context error, but the waits reached through replanContinuation still use context.Background() (also delegation_handoff.go:352), so a cancelled dispatch is not honoured there for up to about two seconds. The new ctx.Err return (review_dispatch.go:2246-2248) is uncovered by the focused tests.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N7\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\".pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-resume-residuals.md\",\"line\":77,\"summary\":\"API/contract changes still says a resume or handoff that meets another's recorded continuation returns that record, which contradicts decision D1 and the code: a continuation of another kind or agent is refused.\"}\n],\n\"prior_findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"R1-N1\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Kind is checked in the take path (review_dispatch.go:2240-2244, continuationKindMismatch 2256-2268), in the resume plan (review_run_continuity.go:440-448) and in the handoff plan (delegation_handoff.go:357-364); the claim-conflict path goes through the plans (review_dispatch.go:776-787). go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose -run RunContinuity -v passes, including the kind-refusal test, which exercises the helper only.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R1-N2\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"review_resume_race_test.go covers the take after a replan and the claim-failure removal (both pass; review_dispatch.go:762-764 and 771-773 covered). The coverage profile of the focused tests shows zero counts for delegation_handoff.go:331-337, 353-364, review_run_continuity.go:440-448 handling of an existing record and review_dispatch.go:777-784; a search of the test files found no end-to-end random-name resume.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R1-N3\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"review_dispatch.go:2246-2248 returns ctx.Err() after the wait; review_run_continuity.go:435 and delegation_handoff.go:352 still pass context.Background().\"},\n{\"id\":\"R1-N4\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"review_dispatch.go:776-781 returns the replan's refusal instead of the publication conflict (established by reading; no focused test reaches it, see R1-N2).\"},\n{\"id\":\"R1-N5\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"git diff db397d16..9ab6f287 shows the added sentence in POSE.md, locales/pt-BR/POSE.md and both embedded copies, and decisions D1 and D2 in spec section 5.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R1-N6\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"review_rounds.go evaluates heldPath once before the switch and uses it in the case and the reason, which now says 'still in use or cannot be checked'.\"}\n],\n\"sweep\":\"The eleven files of the subject: the diff since round 1 in full, the dispatch continuation path, take, claim, wait and kind check, the resume and handoff plans, the round thread selection, the new race tests and their package hooks, the manual in both locales and embedded copies, and the spec's requirements, limit, decisions and trace. Ran the focused tests with coverage, go vet on the two packages and the planned pose checks.\",\n\"criteria\":[\n{\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Checked L1, D1 and D2 against the code. Verified: the runtime directory is created exclusively, the claim is exclusive, and a failed claim removes only the directory this continuation took. L1's two guards fail toward refusing or recording. D2 accepts, as a recorded decision, that a continued session works in a moved directory. L1 no longer covers the untested claim-conflict return, reported in R1-N2.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Lost take and lost claim are exercised by the new race tests, which also pass here; no directory sharing or re-run of a recorded continuation was found. The bounded uncancellable wait is R1-N3.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Resume and handoff now answer a recorded continuation under the same rules as their plans; the stale spec sentence is N7.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Mismatched continuations return actionable refusals and a cancelled take returns the context error; the remaining planning wait is R1-N3.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The CLI consumers already handle plan.Existing and PendingContinuation; signatures changed only inside package pose.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"A moved checkout is recorded in safety.limitations and the thread reason names the held path.\"},\n{\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Examined the CLI resume and handoff answers and the record fields: no schema change, and the new outcomes follow the existing plan refusals stated in D1.\"},\n{\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Read the continuation paths and ran the focused tests; no behavioral defect beyond R1-N3 was established.\"},\n{\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-a7fb2a1d9e87e7a9\",\"rationale\":\"No structural deltas were observed, so there is nothing to map. D1 addresses the cause of the wrong-kind result under R1 by applying the plans' rules after a lost race, and D2 addresses R3 by keeping the reserved attempt usable and recording the move.\"},\n{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Compared the added manual sentence in both locales and the embedded copies with the fallback code; they match. The inconsistency inside the spec is N7.\"},\n{\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Examined the refusal and reason texts: they name the run that continued or the held path, and a cancelled take no longer advises removing a directory.\"},\n{\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"R1-N2\"},\n{\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"The subject's files are those the spec lists, including the new race test; nothing outside R1 to R6 was found in them. The undelivered part of R6 is R1-N2.\"},\n{\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Examined directory derivation, exclusive creation, removal on a lost claim and the test hooks: the hooks are unexported no-ops in production, and no new input crosses a trust boundary.\"},\n{\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"One small helper and two unexported hooks, following the package's existing hook pattern, are the smallest way to share the kind rule and make the races testable. Parallel tests in the package would invalidate the global hooks; none use t.Parallel today.\"}\n],\n\"tools\":[\n{\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-resume-residuals --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-a7fb2a1d9e87e7a9\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0, observed, no deltas.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0 with --no-persist; the gap seen in the output tail concerns an HTTP consumer outside this change.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; the scan reports itself incomplete because two older specs could not be read.\"},\n{\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Ran, exit 1: no approving review, spec not done, and it reports that current semantic inputs are not represented by a sealed bundle. It cannot pass before the attestation.\"},\n{\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Ran, exit 1 with 'current semantic inputs are not represented by a sealed bundle'; it cannot pass before the attestation of this review.\"},\n{\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\"},\n{\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0 with zero findings.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Not rerun: the sealed result covers it. Eight focused internal/cli tests fail in this sandbox; the failure messages seen cite /home ownership blocking task state. internal/pose continuity tests pass.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Not rerun: the sealed result covers it; the same sandbox limitation applies.\"}\n]}\n```\nEOF\ncat \"$TMPDIR/draft.md\" | \"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -; git status --short | head -n 5","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3682,"cache_read_input_tokens":191904,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3682},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"c973acd2-a64a-4a15-aedc-9a78f3d18620","timestamp":"2026-11-28T00:28:31.063Z","request_id":"req_011ChUNwFVzW9E7GDpP2DQtU","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Lf6PMQa6YNRNq6KNVK4GVy":{"command":"cat <<'EOF' > \"$TMPDIR/draft.md\"\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n```pose-draft\n{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"changes-requested\",\n\"findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"R1-N2\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\".pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-resume-residuals.md\",\"line\":129,\"summary\":\"R6 is still traced satisfied but half of it is missing: no test resumes end to end a run with a recorded random runtime name (only the unit naming test), 