ity -v passes, including the kind-refusal test, which exercises the helper only.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R1-N2\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"review_resume_race_test.go covers the take after a replan and the claim-failure removal (both pass; review_dispatch.go:762-764 and 771-773 covered). The coverage profile of the focused tests shows zero counts for delegation_handoff.go:331-337, 353-356 and 357-364 inner branches, review_run_continuity.go:440-448 handling of an existing record and review_dispatch.go:777-784; a search of the test files found no end-to-end random-name resume. The remainder is N7.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R1-N3\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"review_dispatch.go:2246-2248 returns ctx.Err() after the wait; review_run_continuity.go:435 and delegation_handoff.go:352 still pass context.Background(). The remainder is N8.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R1-N4\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"review_dispatch.go:776-781 returns the replan's refusal instead of the publication conflict (established by reading; no focused test reaches it, see N7).\"},\n{\"id\":\"R1-N5\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"git diff db397d16..9ab6f287 shows the added sentence in POSE.md, locales/pt-BR/POSE.md and both embedded copies, and decisions D1 and D2 in spec section 5.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R1-N6\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"review_rounds.go evaluates heldPath once before the switch and uses it in the case and the reason, which now says 'still in use or cannot be checked'.\"}\n],\n\"sweep\":\"The eleven files of the subject: the non-scaffold diff since round 1, the dispatch continuation path, take, claim, wait and kind check, the resume and handoff plans, the round thread selection, the new race tests and their package hooks, the manual in both locales and embedded copies, and the spec's requirements, limit, decisions and trace. Ran the focused tests with coverage, go vet on the two packages and the planned pose checks.\",\n\"criteria\":[\n{\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Checked L1, D1 and D2 against the code. Verified: the runtime directory is created exclusively, the claim is exclusive, and a failed claim removes only the directory this continuation took. L1's two guards fail toward refusing or recording. D2 accepts, as a recorded decision, that a continued session works in a moved directory. L1 no longer covers the untested claim-conflict return, reported in N7.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Lost take and lost claim are exercised by the new race tests, which also pass here; no directory sharing or re-run of a recorded continuation was found. The bounded uncancellable wait is N8.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Resume and handoff now answer a recorded continuation under the same rules as their plans; the stale spec sentence is N9.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Mismatched continuations return actionable refusals and a cancelled take returns the context error; the remaining planning wait is N8.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The CLI consumers already handle plan.Existing and PendingContinuation; signatures changed only inside package pose.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"A moved checkout is recorded in safety.limitations and the thread reason names the held path.\"},\n{\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Examined the CLI resume and handoff answers and the record fields: no schema change, and the new outcomes follow the existing plan refusals stated in D1.\"},\n{\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Read the continuation paths and ran the focused tests; no behavioral defect beyond N8 was established.\"},\n{\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-a7fb2a1d9e87e7a9\",\"rationale\":\"No structural deltas were observed, so there is nothing to map. D1 addresses the cause of the wrong-kind result under R1 by applying the plans' rules after a lost race, and D2 addresses R3 by keeping the reserved attempt usable and recording the move.\"},\n{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Compared the added manual sentence in both locales and the embedded copies with the fallback code; they match. The inconsistency inside the spec is N9.\"},\n{\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Examined the refusal and reason texts: they name the run that continued or the held path, and a cancelled take no longer advises removing a directory.\"},\n{\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N7\"},\n{\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"The subject's files are those the spec lists, including the new race test; nothing outside R1 to R6 was found in them. The undelivered part of R6 is N7.\"},\n{\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Examined directory derivation, exclusive creation, removal on a lost claim and the test hooks: the hooks are unexported no-ops in production, and no new input crosses a trust boundary.\"},\n{\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"One small helper and two unexported hooks, following the package's existing hook pattern, are a small way to share the kind rule and make the races testable. Parallel tests in the package would invalidate the global hooks; a search found no t.Parallel there.\"}\n],\n\"tools\":[\n{\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-resume-residuals --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-a7fb2a1d9e87e7a9\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0, observed, no deltas.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0 with --no-persist; the gap seen in the output tail concerns an HTTP consumer outside this change.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; the scan reports itself incomplete because two older specs could not be read.\"},\n{\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Ran, exit 1: no approving review, spec not done, and it reports that current semantic inputs are not represented by a sealed bundle. It cannot pass before the attestation.\"},\n{\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Ran, exit 1 with 'current semantic inputs are not represented by a sealed bundle'; it cannot pass before the attestation of this review.\"},\n{\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\"},\n{\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0 with zero findings.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Not rerun: the sealed result covers it. Eight focused internal/cli tests fail in this sandbox; the failure messages seen cite /home ownership blocking task state. internal/pose continuity tests pass.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Not rerun: the sealed result covers it; the same sandbox limitation applies.\"}\n]}\n```","ttft_ms":1360,"type":"result","duration_ms":603680,"uuid":"3d41db07-e6b9-425d-af79-3ba43d6b3255","ttft_stream_ms":803,"time_to_request_ms":63,"first_content_frame_ms":803,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":24,"outputTokens":24340,"cacheReadInputTokens":1990982,"cacheCreationInputTokens":64480,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7004662,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":8338,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":64480,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-24T05:32:18.381Z"}
